 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 507019,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What is the sum of the first 100 terms of the arithmetic sequence with first term 4 and constant difference 7?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>You need to know the 100th term.</p>\n<p>You can find any term by using the formula: <span data-math=\"{a_i} = {a_1} + d \\times \\left({i - 1} \\right)\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"{a_{100}} = 4 + 7 \\times \\left({100 - 1} \\right) = 4 + 7(99) = 697\"></span></p>\n<p>The sum of the first <span data-math=\"n\"></span> terms of an arithmetic sequence is: <span data-math=\"{s_n} = n\\left({\\frac{{{a_1} + {a_n}}}{2}} \\right)\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"{s_{100}} = 100\\left({\\frac{{4 + 697}}{2}} \\right) = 100\\left({\\frac{{701}}{2}} \\right) = 35,050\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "35050"
    }
   ],
